# JNLisp CFD Native Display Package

- Author: Jed Nelson  
- Date: [Current]

Native visualization for domains and meshes using Ebitengine.

TODO: Add the `ns` macro to make clear that this requires access
to jnl.cfd.geometry


## Display functions

Shows a domain in a native window. Returns viewer handle.
Window size defaults to 800x600.
j(defn show-domain
  ([domain] (show-domain domain 800 600))
  ([domain width height]
    (.show-domain domain width height)))

Shows a mesh in a native window. Returns viewer handle.
Window size defaults to 800x600.
j(defn show-mesh
  ([mesh] (show-mesh mesh 800 600))
  ([mesh width height]
    (.show-mesh mesh width height)))

Closes the viewer window gracefully.
j(defn close-viewer []
  (.viewer-close))


## Convenience

View whatever geometry object you have.
j(defn view [obj]
  (cond
    (domain? obj) (show-domain obj)
    (mesh? obj) (show-mesh obj)
    :else (throw (ex-info "Cannot view object of type " (type obj)))))
